+# Project Plan
+
+Enhance the Macro Tracker app by adding a Navigation Drawer (Side Menu) with a 'Daily Goal & Profile' section. Here, users specify their dietary preference (e.g., Veg/Non-veg) and their daily activity level (e.g., sedentary, gym-goer). Using this data, the app uses the integrated Gemini AI to smartly suggest meals. Additionally, add a delete button to logged meals so users can easily remove accidental entries.
+
+## Project Brief
+
+# Project Brief: Macro Tracker
+
+## Features
+1. **Profile & Goals Configuration:** A Navigation Drawer (Side Menu) that allows users to quickly configure their dietary preferences (e.g., Veg/Non-veg) and daily activity levels (e.g., sedentary, gym-goer).
+2. **AI-Powered Meal Suggestions:** Integration with Gemini AI to analyze the user's dietary preferences and activity level to provide smart, personalized meal recommendations.
+3. **Meal Logging & Deletion:** An interface for users to review their logged meals, featuring a dedicated delete action to easily remove accidental or unwanted entries.
+
+## High-Level Tech Stack
+* **Language:** Kotlin
+* **UI Toolkit:** Jetpack Compose
+* **Navigation:** Jetpack Navigation 3 (State-driven navigation strategy to handle transitions between the main tracker and the profile/drawer screens)
+* **Adaptive Layouts:** Compose Material Adaptive library (To build a responsive UI, ensuring the Navigation Drawer and main layout adapt gracefully across different device form factors)
+* **Asynchronous Operations:** Kotlin Coroutines (For handling seamless, non-blocking network calls to the AI service)
+* **AI Integration:** Google Gemini API SDK (For fetching intelligent meal suggestions based on user profiles)
+
+## Implementation Steps
+**Total Duration:** 11h 23m 35s
+
+### Task_1_Setup_Data_Layer: Initialize Room database for food logging and configure API clients for Nutrition API and Gemini AI.
+- **Status:** COMPLETED
+- **Updates:** Task 1: Setup Data Layer has been successfully implemented. Added Room database (FoodLogEntity, FoodLogDao, AppDatabase). Added Retrofit, Moshi, and Gemini SDK. Set up OpenFoodFacts client and Gemini client. API keys are configured to be read from local.properties via BuildConfig. Project builds successfully.
+- **Acceptance Criteria:**
+  - Room entities and DAO created
+  - Nutrition API client configured with API_KEY
+  - Gemini API client configured with API_KEY
+  - Project builds successfully
+
+### Task_2_Food_Logging_Feature: Implement Food Search and Logging UI using Jetpack Compose, fetching data from Nutrition API and saving to Room.
+- **Status:** COMPLETED
+- **Updates:** Task 2 implemented successfully. Created FoodViewModel using StateFlow. Created FoodScreen in Jetpack Compose with search text field, lazy column for results, and lazy column for saved foods. Integrated with NutritionApi and Room database. Ensured edge-to-edge support. Project builds successfully.
+- **Acceptance Criteria:**
+  - Search UI displays results from Nutrition API
+  - Selected food items can be saved to local Room DB
+  - UI works without crashing
+
